# Eddi dev2 — kanshi output profile (installed at ~/.config/kanshi/config).
#
# kanshi applies this at session start AND re-applies on monitor hotplug / power-cycle
# (which otherwise re-detects as native landscape and breaks the portrait UI). The panel
# enumerates as HDMI-A-1 on the Pi 5's first micro-HDMI port, HDMI-A-2 on the second — so
# there's a profile for each, and kanshi uses whichever matches the connected port.
# (The labwc autostart ALSO forces transform 90 directly, as a boot-race backstop.)
#
# 800x480 native (landscape); transform 90 presents it as 480x800 portrait. Flip to 270 if
# the panel is mounted the other way.
profile eddi1 {
    output "HDMI-A-1" mode 800x480 position 0,0 scale 1 transform 90
}
profile eddi2 {
    output "HDMI-A-2" mode 800x480 position 0,0 scale 1 transform 90
}
